From e66e7a111583b11af352c53c8f4a3aba0b1eaa04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:07:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 106/106] ChopGimp: fused layer styles
 (chopgimp:layer-style-fused), level-aware stroke

- Piste 8: consecutive layer style filters of a drawable (gegl:dropshadow,
  gegl:inner-glow, chopgimp:stroke) are rendered by one
  chopgimp:layer-style-fused node chained by the filter stack in place of
  the filters' own graphs (gimp_filter_stack_set_fuse_func(),
  gimpdrawable-fused-styles.c). The filters stay separate in the UI, XCF
  and undo. Alpha-only grow/shrink (exact gegl:median-blur quantization),
  same FIR blur on the alpha, glow "median fix" on 9 alpha values, per
  effect planes cached (1-4 bytes/px, cells invalidated by the input's
  changes, computed 256 px ahead), one compositing pass for all effects
  with GIMP's own blend/composite functions. Result equals the chain
  (float: < 0.001/255; 8 bit: <= 1/255, one pixel in 1.4 M at 2/255).
  Not fused: fractional offsets, IIR radius > 40, glow-map options,
  translucent inner glow color, dashed strokes, unsupported blend modes,
  mask / selection region / clip / crop / split preview / component
  restriction, filter being edited or to be merged. Fused filters' own
  caches are off. Rasterize uses the stack output when the top filter is
  fused; merging a single fused filter suspends fusion.
  CHOPGIMP_NO_FUSED_STYLES=1 turns it off, CHOPGIMP_FUSED_STYLES_DEBUG=1
  prints the runs.
- Item 3: chopgimp:stroke renders at mipmap levels (roi in level-0
  coordinates as GEGL gives them, width/dashes/reach scaled, gradient and
  pattern in image coordinates): equal to the stroke of the mipmapped
  layer. Both ops added to the draft (level-aware) list.
- Piste 14: the fused op reads its input in the processing format ("RGBA
  float") and extracts the alpha (babl has no fast path from 8-bit to
  "A float": 3.6x slower), no format conversion between effects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
